The Russian-installed governor of  [LINK: (Kherson Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kherson_Oblast] ,  [LINK: (Vladimir Saldo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Saldo] , said 28 people were killed while several others were injured in a Ukrainian drone strike on hotels and restaurants in  [LINK: (Khorly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Khorly&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A5%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BB%D0%B8] ]. Saldo accused Ukraine of deliberately targeting civilians during  [LINK: (New Year's Eve) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Year%27s_Eve]  celebrations. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-1]

Multiple animals were killed and injured in a Russian airstrike on the  [LINK: (Feldman Ecopark) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feldman_Ecopark]  in  [LINK: (Lisne) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lisne,_Kharkiv_Raion&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9B%D1%96%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%B5_(%D0%A5%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BA%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ],  [LINK: (Kharkiv Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kharkiv_Oblast] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-2]

Drones were reported over  [LINK: (Moscow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow] , shutting down local airports. They were believed to be timed to interfere with President  [LINK: (Putin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Putin] 's New Year's speech. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-3]  Ukrainian drones struck the  [LINK: (Ilsky) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilsky]  oil refinery in  [LINK: (Krasnodar Krai) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krasnodar_Krai]  and various sites in occupied  [LINK: (Donetsk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donetsk_Oblast] . [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-4]

[LINK: (Germany) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germany]  delivered two  [LINK: (Patriot missile systems) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patriot_missile_systems]  to Ukraine. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-5]

Six people were killed in a Russian missile attack on  [LINK: (Kharkiv) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kharkiv] . [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-6]

[LINK: (Kyrylo Budanov) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyrylo_Budanov] , head of the  [LINK: (HUR) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Main_Directorate_of_Intelligence_(Ukraine)] , was appointed to replace  [LINK: (Andriy Yermak) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andriy_Yermak]  as head of the  [LINK: (Office of the President of Ukraine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Office_of_the_President_of_Ukraine] . [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-7]

Ukrainian drones struck the  [LINK: (Novokuybyshevsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novokuybyshevsk]  Oil Refinery in  [LINK: (Samara Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samara_Oblast] . [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-8]

Geolocated footage showed Ukrainian forces operating in  [LINK: (Drobysheve) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drobysheve]  near  [LINK: (Lyman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyman,_Ukraine] , an area Russian forces claimed they controlled. Geolocated footage showed Russian advances in the city of  [LINK: (Kostiantynivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kostiantynivka]  and northwest of the village of  [LINK: (Oleksandro-Kalynove) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oleksandro-Kalynove] ; and Russian advances towards  [LINK: (Hryhorivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hryhorivka,_Zaporizhzhia_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%93%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_(%D0%97%D0%B0%D0%BF%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%96%D0%B7%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ] and  [LINK: (Prymorske) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prymorske,_Zaporizhzhia_Oblast]  near the  [LINK: (Konka river) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konka_(Zaporizhzhia_Oblast)] . [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-9]

In  [LINK: (Dnipropetrovsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dnipropetrovsk_Oblast]  and  [LINK: (Zaporizhzhia Oblasts) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zaporizhzhia_Oblast] , 44 settlements were subjected to mandatory evacuation due to the deteriorating "security situation", affecting some 3,000 children and families. [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-10]

Geolocated footage indicated Russian advances in central  [LINK: (Sotnytskyi Kozachok) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sotnytskyi_Kozachok] , northwest of Kharkiv; and northeast of  [LINK: (Orikhovo-Vasylivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orikhovo-Vasylivka]  near the  [LINK: (E40 highway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_route_E40_in_Ukraine] . [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-11]

The Russian Defense Ministry claimed Russian forces seized  [LINK: (Podoly) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Podoly]  near  [LINK: (Kupiansk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kupiansk] . The  [LINK: (Head of Chechnya) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Head_of_the_Chechen_Republic] ,  [LINK: (Ramzan Kadyrov) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramzan_Kadyrov] , claimed the Chechen  [LINK: (270th Akhmat-Kavkaz Motorized Rifle Regiment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=270th_Akhmat-Kavkaz_Motorized_Rifle_Regiment&action=edit&redlink=1]  took the town of  [LINK: (Bilohiria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Bilohiria,_Zaporizhzhia_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%91%D1%96%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B3%D1%96%D1%80%27%D1%8F_(%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE)] ], southeast of  [LINK: (Orikhiv) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orikhiv] . [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-12]

Russian authorities said two people were killed in Ukrainian drone strikes on  [LINK: (Belgorod) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgorod_Oblast]  and  [LINK: (Kursk Oblasts) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kursk_Oblast] . [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-13]

Two people, including a  [LINK: (National Guard of Ukraine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Guard_of_Ukraine]  officer, were injured in a car bombing in  [LINK: (Obolonskyi District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Obolonskyi_District]  in Kyiv. A suspect was arrested. [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-14]

The  [LINK: (mayor of Moscow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayor_of_Moscow]  claimed around 28 drones approached the city, leading to the cancellation of more than 200 flights as the  [LINK: (Vnukovo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vnukovo_International_Airport] ,  [LINK: (Domodedovo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow_Domodedovo_Airport] , and  [LINK: (Zhukovsky) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhukovsky_International_Airport]  airports were closed. [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-15]  Ukrainian drones struck the Energia enterprise at  [LINK: (Yelets) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yelets]  in  [LINK: (Lipetsk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lipetsk_Oblast] . The plant makes batteries for various Russian weapon systems. [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-16]

President  [LINK: (Zelenskyy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volodymyr_Zelenskyy]  dismissed Lieutenant General  [LINK: (Serhii Deineko) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serhii_Deineko]  as head of the  [LINK: (State Border Guard Service of Ukraine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_Border_Guard_Service_of_Ukraine] , and replaced him on an interim basis with his deputy  [LINK: (Valeriy Vavrynyuk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valeriy_Vavrynyuk] . [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-17]

[LINK: (Vasyl Malyuk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vasyl_Malyuk]  was forced to resign as head of the  [LINK: (SBU) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Security_Service_of_Ukraine]  by President Zelenskyy. [LINK: ([18]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-18]

One person was killed in a Russian drone attack on Kyiv. [LINK: ([19]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-19]

Russia claimed to have taken  [LINK: (Hrabovske) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hrabovske]  in Sumy Oblast. [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-20]

Ukrainian drones destroyed a Russian  [LINK: (9S32M1 radar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/9S32]  of an  [LINK: (S-300V) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S-300V]  missile system in Donetsk Oblast. [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-21]

The Russian  [LINK: (136th Separate Guards Motor Rifle Brigade) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/136th_Separate_Guards_Motor_Rifle_Brigade] ’s commander, Colonel  [LINK: (Eric Selimov) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Eric_Selimov&action=edit&redlink=1] , was killed in a car crash in  [LINK: (Alchevsk Raion) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alchevsk_Raion]  in  [LINK: (Luhansk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luhansk_Oblast] . [LINK: ([22]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-22]

Ukrainian military observer  [LINK: (Kostyantyn Mashovets) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kostyantyn_Mashovets&action=edit&redlink=1]  reported Russian advances north of Yablunivka across  [LINK: (Highway H20) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highway_H20_(Ukraine)] , and also in southeast Kostiantynivka. [LINK: ([23]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-23]

A Russian milblogger claimed Russian forces took the town of  [LINK: (Pishchane) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pishchane,_Kharkiv_Oblast] , southeast of Kupiansk. [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-january-6-2026-24]

Ukrainian drones struck targets in  [LINK: (Penza) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penza]  and  [LINK: (Sterlitamak) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sterlitamak] . [LINK: ([25]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-25]  Ukrainian drones struck  [LINK: (Yaroslavl) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yaroslavl] , with Yaroslavl Oil Refinery believed to be the target. [LINK: ([26]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-26]  Ukrainian forces attacked the 100th Arsenal of the  [LINK: (Main Missile and Artillery Directorate) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Main_Missile_and_Artillery_Directorate]  located in  [LINK: (Neya) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neya_(town)]  in  [LINK: (Kostroma Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kostroma_Oblast] , which supplied ammunitions storages in the  [LINK: (Central) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Military_District]  and  [LINK: (Moscow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow_Military_District]  military districts. Ukrainian forces also attacked an oil depot in  [LINK: (Usmansky District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usmansky_District]  in  [LINK: (Lipetsk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lipetsk_Oblast] . [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-january-6-2026-24]

Ukrainian drones set fire to the  [LINK: (Oskolneftesnab oil depot) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Oskolneftesnab_oil_depot&action=edit&redlink=1]  near  [LINK: (Kotel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kotel,_Belgorod_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  in Belgorod Oblast. A warehouse belonging to the Russian  [LINK: (20th Motor Rifle Division) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=20th_Motor_Rifle_Division&action=edit&redlink=1]  in  [LINK: (Donetsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donetsk]  was also struck. [LINK: ([27]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-27]

Russian forces struck  [LINK: (Chornomorsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_of_Chornomorsk]  and  [LINK: (Pivdennyi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pivdennyi_Port]  ports in  [LINK: (Odesa Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odesa_Oblast] , killing one person and injuring five more. [LINK: ([28]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-28]

Geolocated footage showed Russian advances in north  [LINK: (Yunakivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yunakivka]  and Ukrainian advances in  [LINK: (Vovchanski Khutory) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vovchanski_Khutory] . [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-29]

Russian forces struck  [LINK: (Lviv) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lviv]  with an  [LINK: (Oreshnik) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oreshnik_(missile)]  missile. [LINK: ([30]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-january-9-2026-30]

DeepstateUA reported Russian forces took the towns of  [LINK: (Andriivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andriivka,_Sumy_Raion]  in Sumy Oblast and  [LINK: (Novomarkove) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Novomarkove&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B5] ] in Donetsk Oblast. [LINK: ([31]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-31]  The Ukrainian  [LINK: (Kursk Group of Forces) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Kursk_Group_of_Forces&action=edit&redlink=1]  denied the claim of Andriivka being captured. [LINK: ([32]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-32]

A  [LINK: (Russian shadow fleet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_shadow_fleet]  oil tanker Elbus was struck by a drone off the coast of Turkey. According to ASTRA, the tanker was headed to  [LINK: (Novorossiysk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novorossiysk]  and sustained damage, but no crew members were injured. The ship was towed to  [LINK: (İnebolu) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C4%B0nebolu]  for inspections. [LINK: ([33]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-33]

The pro-Ukrainian  [LINK: (Freedom of Russia Legion) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freedom_of_Russia_Legion]  set fire to some 15 trucks at the village of  [LINK: (Kochegury) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kochegury]  in Belgorod Oblast. [LINK: ([34]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-34]

Geolocated footage showed Ukrainian forces continued to operate in  [LINK: (Zahryzove) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Zahryzove&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%97%D0%B0%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B7%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B5] ] near  [LINK: (Borova) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borova,_Izium_Raion,_Kharkiv_Oblast] , an area Russian forces claimed they controlled, while the Russian Defense Ministry claimed Russian forces took the town of  [LINK: (Bratske) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Bratske,_Synelnykove_Raion,_Dnipropetrovsk_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%91%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B5_(%D0%A1%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ], south of  [LINK: (Pokrovske) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pokrovske,_Synelnykove_Raion,_Dnipropetrovsk_Oblast] . [LINK: ([35]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-35]

Four people were killed in Russian airstrikes on Kyiv that also damaged the building housing the Qatari embassy. [LINK: ([36]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-36]

Ukrainian  [LINK: (FP-2 drones) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukrspecsystems_PD-2]  struck a fuel train in Crimea and a military arms depot in Donetsk. [LINK: ([37]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-37]  Ukrainian missiles struck the thermal power plants at  [LINK: (Belgorod) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgorod]  and  [LINK: (Oryol) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oryol] , resulting in blackouts. [LINK: ([38]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-38]

The Minister for Development of Communities and Territories  [LINK: (Oleksiy Kuleba) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oleksiy_Kuleba] , said Russian forces struck a vessel en route to  [LINK: (Chornomorsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chornomorsk] , and another vessel near Odesa, killing a  [LINK: (Syrian) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrians]  national. [LINK: ([39]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-39]

Russian milbloggers claimed Russian forces took the town of  [LINK: (Tyshchenkivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Tyshchenkivka&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A2%D0%B8%D1%89%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0] ], northwest of Kupiansk. Geolocated footage showed Russian advances in west  [LINK: (Novomarkove) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Novomarkove&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B5] ], and northwest of  [LINK: (Stupochky) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Stupochky&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D1%82%D1%83%D0%BF%D0%BE%D1%87%D0%BA%D0%B8] ] and  [LINK: (Ivanopillia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ivanopillia&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%86%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BF%D1%96%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8F] ], all located east of Kostiantynivka. Geolocated footage showed Ukrainian advances west of  [LINK: (Pryluky) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Pryluky,_Polohy_Raion&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9F%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%BA%D0%B8_(%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B3%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ] and Russian infiltration in  [LINK: (Zelene) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Zelene,_Polohy_Raion&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%97%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B5_(%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B3%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ], both located north of  [LINK: (Huliaipole) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huliaipole] . Geolocated footage showed Ukrainian forces continued to operate in central  [LINK: (Stepnohirsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stepnohirsk] , an area Russian forces claimed they controlled. [LINK: ([30]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-january-9-2026-30]

The SBU arrested two  [LINK: (GRU) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GRU_(Russian_Federation)]  agents who were accused of assessing the effectiveness of the  [LINK: (Oreshnik missile) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oreshnik_missile]  strike on Lviv. [LINK: ([40]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-40]

Ukrainian drones set fire to the  [LINK: (Volgograd) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volgograd]  oil refinery. [LINK: ([41]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-41]  A drone warehouse in Zaporizhzhia Oblast, attached to the Russian  [LINK: (19th Motor Rifle Division) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/19th_Motor_Rifle_Division] , was attacked, as was an "UAV control point" near  [LINK: (Pokrovsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pokrovsk] . In Donetsk Oblast, a command post in  [LINK: (Kurakhivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kurakhivka]  and a grouping of the  [LINK: (76th Guards Air Assault Division) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/76th_Guards_Air_Assault_Division]  in  [LINK: (Hirnyk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hirnyk,_Donetsk_Oblast]  were both attacked. [LINK: ([42]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-42]   [LINK: (Voronezh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voronezh]  was attacked by 70 drones and a  [LINK: (Neptune missile) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neptune_missile]  according to the SHOT Telegram channel, while the Russian MoD claimed all were shot down. The air defense and 20 explosions caused by the drones lasted for an hour. [LINK: ([43]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-43]

[LINK: (Iraq) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraq%E2%80%93Russia_relations]  established a commission to prevent Iraqi nationals from going to Russia to fight in Ukraine. [LINK: ([44]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-44]

Russian milbloggers claimed Russian forces seized  [LINK: (Viroliubivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viroliubivka] , north of Kostiantynivka, and the towns of  [LINK: (Dobropillia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Dobropillia,_Polohy_Raion,_Zaporizhzhia_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BF%D1%96%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8F_(%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B3%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ] and  [LINK: (Svyatopetrivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Svyatopetrivka&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D0%B2%D1%8F%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%B5%D1%82%D1%80%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0] ], both located north of Huliaipole. [LINK: ([45]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-45]

[LINK: (Voronezh Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voronezh_Oblast]  Governor  [LINK: (Alexander Gusev) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleksandr_Gusev_(politician)]  claimed a woman died and three were injured by a drone attack on Voronezh city. The Governor claimed several administrative buildings, a secondary school, ten private houses and ten apartment blocks were damaged in “one of the heaviest drone attacks since the start of the special military operation.” [LINK: ([46]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-46]

Russia deployed a new jet powered drone called the Geran-5, which carries a 90 kg (200 lb) warhead, has a strike range of 1,000 km (620 mi) and can be air launched by  [LINK: (Su-25) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sukhoi_Su-25]  aircraft according to HUR. [LINK: ([47]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-47]

Ukrainian drones struck three  [LINK: (Lukoil) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lukoil]  drilling rigs on the  [LINK: (Caspian Sea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caspian_Sea]  (the V. Filanovsky, Yuri Korchagin, and Valeri Graifer), a  [LINK: (Buk-M3) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buk-M1]  missile system in Luhansk Oblast, and a Russian army warehouse in Kherson Oblast. [LINK: ([48]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-48]

Britain said it will develop a new  [LINK: (ballistic missile) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nightfall_(missile)]  for the defense of Ukraine. [LINK: ([49]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-49]

Geolocated footage showed Russian infiltration in south Podoly near Kupiansk, and Russian advances in east Kostyantynivka, and in west  [LINK: (Ridkodub) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ridkodub,_Kramatorsk_Raion&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A0%D1%96%D0%B4%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B4%D1%83%D0%B1_(%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ] near Borova. [LINK: ([50]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-50]

Ukrainian drones struck the  [LINK: (Novocherkassk Thermal Power Plant) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Novocherkassk_Thermal_Power_Plant&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (ru) -> https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%8F_%D0%93%D0%A0%D0%AD%D0%A1] ] in  [LINK: (Novocherkassk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novocherkassk] ,  [LINK: (Rostov Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rostov_Oblast] , causing a power outage in the region. [LINK: ([51]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-51]

Russian forces struck energy infrastructure in  [LINK: (Odesa Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odesa_Oblast] , causing significant damage and leaving 33,500 consumers without electricity. [LINK: ([52]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-52]  Russian forces also struck two vessels near Odesa Oblast, injuring one person. [LINK: ([53]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-53]

The Russian defense ministry claimed that Russian forces took the town of  [LINK: (Novoboikivske) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Novoboikivske&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B9%D0%BA%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B5] ], east of  [LINK: (Stepnohirsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stepnohirsk] , Zaporizhzhia Oblast. [LINK: ([54]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-54]

Four people were killed in a Russian missile attack in Kharkiv. [LINK: ([55]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-55]

The SBU said it had carried out an attack on a Russian UAV factory in  [LINK: (Taganrog) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taganrog]  in cooperation with the  [LINK: (Ukrainian Navy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukrainian_Navy] . [LINK: ([56]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-56]

Three Greek-owned tankers, the Delta Harmony, the Matilda and the Delta Supreme, were attacked and damaged by unknown maritime drones en route to the  [LINK: (Caspian Pipeline Consortium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caspian_Pipeline_Consortium]  at  [LINK: (Novorossiysk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novorossiysk] . [LINK: ([57]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-57]

A Russian air defence missile accidentally struck an apartment block in  [LINK: (Rostov-on-Don) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rostov-on-Don] , starting a fire. Mayor  [LINK: (Alexander Skryabin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Alexander_Skryabin_(Mayor)&action=edit&redlink=1]  blamed the fire on "Ukrainian drone debris." [LINK: ([58]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-58]  The city was targeted by Ukrainian drones and missiles with the city’s fuel storage tank being reported as on fire. [LINK: ([59]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-59]  The Governor of Rostov Oblast,  [LINK: (Yury Slyusar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yury_Slyusar] , claimed one was killed and five were injured, including a four-year-old, from falling drone debris. [LINK: ([60]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-60]   The Governor of Belgorod Oblast claimed two people were killed in drone strikes. [LINK: ([61]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-61]

The Russian defense ministry claimed that Russian forces crossed the  [LINK: (international border) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia%E2%80%93Ukraine_border]  into Sumy Oblast and took the town of  [LINK: (Komarivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Komarivka,_Shostka_Raion,_Sumy_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_(%D0%A8%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ]. [LINK: ([62]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-62]

President Zelenskyy declared a state of emergency in the Ukrainian energy sector due to Russian attacks and adverse winter conditions. [LINK: ([63]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-63]

Ukrainian drones set fire to the  [LINK: (Nevinnomyssk Azot) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Nevinnomyssk_Azot&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (ru) -> https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%8B%D1%81%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%90%D0%B7%D0%BE%D1%82] ] chemical plant in  [LINK: (Nevinnomyssk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nevinnomyssk] ,  [LINK: (Stavropol Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stavropol_Oblast] . The plant manufacturer made ingredients for explosives, such as  [LINK: (TNT) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TNT]  and  [LINK: (RDX) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RDX] , used by the Russian military. This marked the fifth time the plant had been struck since June 2025. [LINK: ([64]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-64]

The  [LINK: (mayor of Kharkiv) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayor_of_Kharkiv] ,  [LINK: (Ihor Terekhov) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ihor_Terekhov] , claimed that a major critical energy infrastructure facility was destroyed by a Russian strike. [LINK: ([65]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-65]

Russian forces struck the port of Chornomorsk, damaging a docked vessel. [LINK: ([66]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-66]

DeepstateUA reported that Russian forces took the town of  [LINK: (Krasnohirske) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Krasnohirske&action=edit&redlink=1]  in Zaporizhzhia Oblast. [LINK: ([67]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-67]

A Ukrainian drone struck a high-rise building in  [LINK: (Ryazan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryazan] , damaging two apartments and injuring two people. Drone debris also struck an "industrial enterprise" according to Ryazan Governor  [LINK: (Pavel Malkov) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pavel_Malkov] . [LINK: ([68]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-68]

Geolocated footage published on January 16 confirmed Russia's control over  [LINK: (Dobropillia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Dobropillia,_Polohy_Raion,_Zaporizhzhia_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BF%D1%96%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8F_(%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B3%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ].  [LINK: (ISW) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Institute_for_the_Study_of_War]  assessed that Russian forces also took  [LINK: (Varvarivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Varvarivka,_Polohy_Raion,_Zaporizhzhia_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%92%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_(%D0%9F%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B3%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ]; both are located north of Huliaipole. Russian milbloggers claimed that Russian forces took the towns of  [LINK: (Pavlivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Pavlivka,_Vasylivka_Raion,_Zaporizhzhia_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9F%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BB%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_(%D0%92%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ] near Stepnohirsk, and  [LINK: (Kruhle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Pavlivka,_Chuhuiv_Raion,_Kharkiv_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9A%D1%80%D1%83%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B5_(%D0%A7%D1%83%D0%B3%D1%83%D1%97%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ] in Kharkiv Oblast near the international border. The Russian defense ministry claimed that Russian forces took the towns of  [LINK: (Zakitne) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Zakitne&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%97%D0%B0%D0%BA%D1%96%D1%82%D0%BD%D0%B5] ] near Siversk and  [LINK: (Olenokostyantynivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Olenokostyantynivka&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9E%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BA%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8F%D0%BD%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0] ] near Huliaipole. [LINK: ([69]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-69]

The Russian defense ministry claimed that Russian forces took the town of  [LINK: (Pryvillia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pryvillia,_Bakhmut_Raion,_Donetsk_Oblast] , south of  [LINK: (Rai-Oleksandrivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Rai-Oleksandrivka,_Kramatorsk_Raion,_Donetsk_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A0%D0%B0%D0%B9-%D0%9E%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B4%D1%80%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_(%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ], Donetsk Oblast. [LINK: ([70]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-70]

Russian milbloggers claimed that Russian forces took the towns of  [LINK: (Ozerne) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ozerne,_Donetsk_Oblast] , near  [LINK: (Lyman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyman,_Ukraine]  and  [LINK: (Novyi Donbas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Novyi_Donbas&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B1%D0%B0%D1%81] ], east of  [LINK: (Dobropillia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dobropillia] . [LINK: ([71]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-71]

Ukrainian drones strikes on electricity infrastructure in Russian-occupied Ukraine left over 200,000 households in Zaporizhzhia Oblast without power, according to Russian occupation officials. [LINK: ([72]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-72]

The container ship Aurelia was struck by a drone some eighty to ninety nautical miles at sea, after its departure from the Russian port of  [LINK: (Novorossiysk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novorossiysk] . The strike severely damaged several containers but didn’t damage the ship or injury to crew. It stopped at the Turkish port of  [LINK: (Samsun) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samsun]  to have the damaged containers removed. [LINK: ([73]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-73]

Russian forces launched three airstrikes on Kharkiv's  [LINK: (Slobidskyi District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slobidskyi_District] , killing one person and injuring 11 more. [LINK: ([74]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-74]

The Ukrainian military said it had carried out an attack that destroyed a Russian drone warehouse in  [LINK: (Novokrasnianka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Novokrasnianka&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D1%8F%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B0] ], Luhansk Oblast. [LINK: ([75]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-75]

The SBU captured a Russian officer accused of executing nine Ukrainian POWs in Kursk Oblast in 2024. [LINK: ([76]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-76]

The DTEK Energot power plant in  [LINK: (Belgorod) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgorod]  was set on fire by a drone and missile attack but without interruption to power supplies. In  [LINK: (Oryol) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oryol]  the local thermal power plant was struck by drones resulting in some 10 explosions with blackouts in parts of the city. [LINK: ([77]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-77]

Ukrainian drones struck  [LINK: (Adygea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adygea] ; the head of the republic,  [LINK: (Murat Kumpilov) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murat_Kumpilov]  claimed that one person was killed and 13 people, including two children, were injured after a drone was detected in  [LINK: (Novaya Adygea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novaya_Adygea] ,  [LINK: (Takhtamukaysky District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Takhtamukaysky_District] . A fire broke out at an apartment building and a parking lot. [LINK: ([78]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-78]  [LINK: ([79]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-79]  However Telegram channel ASTRA said "debris (was) consistent with an air defense interceptor". A refinery caught fire in  [LINK: (Afipsky) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afipsky] ,  [LINK: (Krasnodar Krai) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krasnodar_Krai] . [LINK: ([80]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-80]  In the evening, another drone strike on an oil terminal near  [LINK: (Volna) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Volna,_Krasnodar_Krai&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (ru) -> https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%92%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BD%D0%B0_(%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9)] ], Krasnodar Krai, killed three people. [LINK: ([81]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-81]

[LINK: (Japan announced) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan%E2%80%93Ukraine_relations]  $6 billion in "humanitarian and technical support" aid for Ukraine, largely for generators and other equipment used for electrical systems such as transformers. [LINK: ([82]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-82]

The  [LINK: (State Investigation Bureau) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_Bureau_of_Investigation_(Ukraine)]  (DBR) arrested a Ukrainian military officer in Sumy Oblast on "suspicion of abusing and torturing subordinates" and threatening to shoot soldiers who failed to follow his orders. [LINK: ([83]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-83]

The Second Western District Military Court in  [LINK: (Moscow) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow]  sentenced Uzbek national Akhmadzhon Kurbonov to life imprisonment for the assassination of Lieutenant General  [LINK: (Igor Kirillov) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Igor_Kirillov_(general)]  in 2024, which Russia blamed on a Ukrainian national. [LINK: ([84]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-84]

The Ukrainian military said it had carried out strikes on three radar stations in Crimea, a drone storage facility in  [LINK: (Novohryhorivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novohryhorivka] , Kherson Oblast, and other Russian military facilities in  [LINK: (Selydove) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selydove]  and  [LINK: (Debaltseve) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debaltseve]  in Donetsk Oblast. [LINK: ([85]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-85]

In Moscow, the Second  [LINK: (Western District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Military_District]  Military Court formally acknowledged that the  [LINK: (Russian cruiser Moskva) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_cruiser_Moskva]  was  [LINK: (sunk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinking_of_the_Moskva]  by a Ukrainian missile, and accused  [LINK: (Andrii Shubin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Andrii_Shubin&action=edit&redlink=1] , then commander of the  [LINK: (406th Artillery Brigade) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/406th_Marine_Artillery_Brigade_(Ukraine)]  of the  [LINK: (Ukrainian Navy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukrainian_Navy] , of giving the orders that led to the sinking of the Moskva. Updated casualties were listed as 20 crew members killed, 24 injured and eight missing. Shubin was also accused of destroying the frigate  [LINK: (Admiral Essen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_frigate_Admiral_Essen]  in April 2022, for which the court demanded 2.2 billion rubles (approximately $28.4 million) in damages. [LINK: ([86]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-86]  Shubin was sentenced to life imprisonment in absentia for terrorism charges related to the sinking. [LINK: ([87]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-87]

The  [LINK: (Penzanefteprodukt oil depot) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Penzanefteprodukt_oil_depot&action=edit&redlink=1]  in  [LINK: (Penza) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penza]  was set on fire by a Ukrainian drone attack, while a private home was set on fire in Voronezh Oblast according to the local governor,  [LINK: (Oleg Melnichenko) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oleg_Melnichenko] . [LINK: ([88]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-january-23-2026-88]  [LINK: ([89]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-89]

The Russian Ministry of Defense and Russian milbloggers claimed that Russian forces took the town of  [LINK: (Symynivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Symynivka&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0] ] near  [LINK: (Vovchansk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vovchansk] . A Russian milblogger claimed that Russian forces took the towns of  [LINK: (Novoselivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Novoselivka,_Velykomykhailivka_rural_hromada,_Synelnykove_Raion,_Dnipropetrovsk_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_(%D0%92%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B8%D1%85%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BB%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D1%81%D1%96%D0%BB%D1%8C%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%B0)] ],  [LINK: (Vorone) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Vorone,_Synelnykove_Raion,_Dnipropetrovsk_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%92%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5_(%D0%A1%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ],  [LINK: (Sosnivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Sosnivka,_Synelnykove_Raion,_Dnipropetrovsk_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BD%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_(%D0%A1%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ], and  [LINK: (Orestopil) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Orestopil&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%91%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%BD_%D0%9E%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BF%D1%96%D0%BB%D1%8C] ], all southeast of  [LINK: (Oleksandrivka, Dnipropetrovsk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Oleksandrivka,_Dnipropetrovsk_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1] . [LINK: ([88]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-january-23-2026-88]

According to the regional governor  [LINK: (Vyacheslav Gladkov) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vyacheslav_Gladkov] , Belgorod Oblast suffered its "most massive" attack that involved that HIMARS, damaging electrical infrastructure, a utility building, a car park and homes in the village of  [LINK: (Tavrovo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tavrovo] . [LINK: ([90]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-90]  Unidentified drones also struck  [LINK: (Taganrog) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taganrog]  in Rostov Oblast, with the city losing power after explosions and fires were reported by locals with a transformer failing. Explosions were also reported in  [LINK: (Oryol) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oryol]  and  [LINK: (Bryansk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bryansk_Oblast] . [LINK: ([91]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-91]

A Russian drone attack damaged two buildings of the  [LINK: (Kyiv Pechersk Lavra) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyiv_Pechersk_Lavra] , the first time the complex sustained war-related damage since  [LINK: (World War II) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_II] . [LINK: ([92]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-92]

An oil refinery in  [LINK: (Slavyansk-on-Kuban) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slavyansk-on-Kuban]  was attacked by Ukrainian drones with at least one oil storage tank being set on fire. The  [LINK: (Novokuybyshevsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novokuybyshevsk]  Oil Refinery in Samara Oblast was also attacked. [LINK: ([93]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-93]

Three people were killed in a Russian drone attack on  [LINK: (Odesa) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odesa] . [LINK: ([94]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-94]  Two others were killed in a separate attack in  [LINK: (Sloviansk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sloviansk] , while a drone strike on a train in Kharkiv Oblast killed five. Additional strikes killed two people in Zaporizhzhia and Kherson Oblasts. [LINK: ([95]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-95]

Two people were killed in a Russian air attack on  [LINK: (Bilohorodka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bilohorodka] ,  [LINK: (Kyiv Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyiv_Oblast] . [LINK: ([96]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-96]

[LINK: (Atesh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atesh]  partisans claimed to have set fire to an electrical substation in  [LINK: (Izhevsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Izhevsk] ,  [LINK: (Udmurtia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Udmurtia] , cutting electricity to the BUMMASH metallurgical plant. [LINK: ([97]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-97]

Ukrainian forces struck the  [LINK: (Khokholskaya) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khokholsky_District]  oil depot in  [LINK: (Voronezh Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voronezh_Oblast]  with thick smoke being spotted over the depot. Ukrainian forces struck Russian soldiers in  [LINK: (Kolotilovka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kolotilovka] ,  [LINK: (Belgorod Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgorod_Oblast] . Other groupings of Russian soldiers were attacked in  [LINK: (Velyka Novosilka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velyka_Novosilka] ,  [LINK: (Shakhove) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Shakhove&action=edit&redlink=1] , and  [LINK: (Hryhoriivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hryhoriivka&action=edit&redlink=1] ,  [LINK: (Donetsk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donetsk_Oblast] . A UAV control center near  [LINK: (Velyka Novosilka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velyka_Novosilka]  and battalion command post near  [LINK: (Berezove) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berezove,_Synelnykove_Raion,_Dnipropetrovsk_Oblast] , both in Russian-occupied  [LINK: (Dnipropetrovsk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dnipropetrovsk_Oblast]  was attacked as was an ammunition depot in  [LINK: (Nyzhnia Duvanka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyzhnia_Duvanka] , Russian-occupied  [LINK: (Luhansk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luhansk_Oblast] . [LINK: ([98]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-98]

Ukrainian officials claimed that Russian forces lost a  [LINK: (Su-34) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Su-34]  and a  [LINK: (Su-30) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Su-30] , without providing further details. On social media a Su-34 was reported destroyed along with its crew. [LINK: ([99]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-99]

Three people were killed in a Russian drone strike in Zaporizhzhia Oblast. [LINK: ([100]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-100]

The bodies of 1,000 Ukrainian soldiers killed in action were repatriated by Russia in exchange for those of 38 Russian soldiers. [LINK: ([101]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-101]

The Russian Defense Ministry claimed that Russian forces took the town of  [LINK: (Bila Bereza) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Bila_Bereza&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%91%D1%96%D0%BB%D0%B0_%D0%91%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%B7%D0%B0] ], east of  [LINK: (Komarivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Komarivka,_Shostka_Raion,_Sumy_Oblast&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%96%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_(%D0%A8%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD)] ] in Sumy Oblast. [LINK: ([102]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-102]

One person was killed by Russian shelling in  [LINK: (Kherson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kherson] . [LINK: ([103]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-103]

The Kremlin said that President Putin agreed to U.S. President Donald Trump's personal request to halt strikes in Kyiv until 1 February to create "favourable conditions" for peace negotiations. [LINK: ([104]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-104]

Near  [LINK: (Stepnohirsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stepnohirsk] , geolocated footage showed that Russian forces took the town of  [LINK: (Lukianivske) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lukianivske&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9B%D1%83%D0%BA%27%D1%8F%D0%BD%D1%96%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B5] ] and the Russian defense ministry claimed that Russian forces took the town of  [LINK: (Richne) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Richne&action=edit&redlink=1]  [ [LINK: (uk) -> https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A0%D1%96%D1%87%D0%BD%D0%B5_(%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%89%D0%B5)] ] as well as  [LINK: (Ternuvate) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ternuvate]  north of Huliaipole. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-105]

Ukrainian forces claimed to have destroyed a  [LINK: (TOR-M1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TOR-M1]  near the village of  [LINK: (Kamianka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kamianka] ,  [LINK: (Luhansk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luhansk_Oblast] . Attacks were also made in  [LINK: (Zaporizhzhia Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zaporizhzhia_Oblast]  on "concentrations of enemy personnel" near  [LINK: (Rivnopillia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Rivnopillia&action=edit&redlink=1] ,  [LINK: (Pryvillia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pryvillia] , and  [LINK: (Uspenivka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Uspenivka&action=edit&redlink=1] , as well as a Russian logistics depot near Voskresenka and a Russian command post in Rivnopillia. Attacks were also made in  [LINK: (Donetsk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donetsk_Oblast]  on troop concentrations near  [LINK: (Chasiv Yar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chasiv_Yar]  and a motorized rifle regiment command post in  [LINK: (Poltavka) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poltavka] , and a UAV command post near  [LINK: (Sluchovsk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Sluchovsk&action=edit&redlink=1] ,  [LINK: (Bryansk Oblast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bryansk_Oblast] . [LINK: ([106]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(1_January_2026_%E2%80%93_present)#cite_note-106]


